      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2528438831,
          "type": null,
          "body": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/wsutil/win32-utils.c#L222  \n```\n            ws_log(LOG_DOMAIN_CAPTURE, LOG_LEVEL_DEBUG, \"Could not create child cleanup job object: %s\",\n                win32strerror(GetLastError()));\n```\n\nThis works in a production (non DEBUG) build so it's not exactly valid to say there are no DEBUG level messages without a special build.  \n  \nIn the first version of !19958, it shows `[Extcap DEBUG]` output by a normal build.  \n  \nHow do we differentiate between debug messages during the coding process vs a DEBUG level log message?",
